[2m│[0m [1m[38;5;231mGiven that a sync hash of a username is brute-forceable, how should userRef work?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mRandom session id (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mNo derivation from the username; log store holds zero personal data. User quotes a session id from the error UI for
[39m     [38;5;246msupport. Loses cross-session user correlation.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Salted FNV-1a of username
     [38;5;246mKeeps cross-session correlation and matches what you picked earlier. Pseudonymous, not anonymous — brute-forceable
[39m     [38;5;246magainst a known user list, and still personal data under GDPR.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Both: session id + salted hash
     [38;5;246mFull correlation power, but reintroduces the personal-data exposure you were avoiding. Only worth it if user-level
[39m     [38;5;246mhistory is a hard support requirement.[39m
